r understands one’s ideas until someone else explains them to you. I suspected at the time that the comment was intended to be gentl…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://daviddfriedman.substack.com/p/implications-of-coase-for-law?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://daviddfriedman.substack.com/p/implications-of-coase-for-law?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/public-choice-links-422026">Public Choice Links, 3/30/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://daviddfriedman.substack.com/p/implications-of-coase-for-law?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://daviddfriedman.substack.com/p/implications-of-coase-for-law?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Mon, 30 Mar 2026 12:31:27 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[How to Disagree Better]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>How to Disagree Better, out this week, and is a brilliant, must-read by Julia Minson, a Professor of Public Policy at the Harvard Kennedy School of Government and the founder of Disagreeing Better, LLC–a behavioral science consultancy and training firm…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://annieduke.substack.com/p/how-to-disagree-better?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://annieduke.substack.com/p/how-to-disagree-better?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/political-psychology-links-3292026">Political Psychology Links, 3/29/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://annieduke.substack.com/p/how-to-disagree-better?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://annieduke.substack.com/p/how-to-disagree-better?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Sun, 29 Mar 2026 12:02:54 GMT</pubD